-- A lifecycle point is a property of the RUN, not of the rule: each entry
-- into a continuation carries its own (EVERY-EACH-QUANTIFIER-SPEC §2.6, card
-- B5, RULED 2026-09-21: binders take their value per instance).
--
-- One rule, two runs. Bob does exactly the same thing in both — he notes on
-- day 9 — and only Alice's cure moves. THE JOIN is the instant Alice's
-- obligation was met, so Bob's deadline follows it.

IMPORT prelude

DECLARE Actor IS ONE OF
    Person HAS who IS A STRING
DECLARE Action IS ONE OF
    Cure HAS by IS AN Actor
    Note HAS by IS AN Actor

alice MEANS Person "Alice"
bob   MEANS Person "Bob"

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`note within 3 of the cure` MEANS
    PARTY alice MUST Cure alice WITHIN 10
    HENCE (PARTY bob MUST Note bob WITHIN 3 OF THE JOIN)

-- Alice cures on day 2: Bob's note is due on day 5, so day 9 is late.
#TRACE `note within 3 of the cure` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Cure alice AT 2
  PARTY bob   DOES Note bob   AT 9

-- Alice cures on day 7: due on day 10, so the same note on day 9 is in time.
#TRACE `note within 3 of the cure` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Cure alice AT 7
  PARTY bob   DOES Note bob   AT 9

-- The residual after each cure prints the anchor as written, not a number:
-- the instant it names is the run's.
#TRACE `note within 3 of the cure` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Cure alice AT 2
